From ece26d18af56de55ac0f108ecede14e4771b0040 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:47:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] ipa: softisp: imx681: Limit the exposure time before
 raising gain

Expose up to 1/60 s, then raise the analogue gain to its maximum, and only
then expose longer. Short exposures limit motion blur on the front camera,
whose AGC would otherwise sit at a full-frame exposure before using any
gain.

This used to be an exposureGainThreshold parameter added to the simple
IPA's own AGC. Since the soft ISP AGC moved to libipa's AgcAlgorithm, the
AeExposureMode stages in the tuning file do the same thing.
---
 src/ipa/softisp/data/imx681.yaml | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ipa/softisp/data/imx681.yaml b/src/ipa/softisp/data/imx681.yaml
index f2bfac6..7125165 100644
--- a/src/ipa/softisp/data/imx681.yaml
+++ b/src/ipa/softisp/data/imx681.yaml
@@ -13,4 +13,11 @@ algorithms:
   # enabling Ccm. The generic identity matrix is not a calibration.
   - Adjust:
   - Agc:
+      # Limit motion blur: expose up to 1/60 s, then raise the analogue gain
+      # to its 16x maximum, and only then expose longer (up to the sensor's
+      # limit).
+      AeExposureMode:
+        Normal:
+          exposureTime: [ 16667, 1000000 ]
+          gain: [ 16.0, 16.0 ]
 ...
